ne\",\"children\":\"research.opena2a.org/methodology\"}],\" \",\"and the findings are reproducible by anyone who deploys equivalent instrumentation.\"]}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"text-gray-300 text-sm mb-3\",\"children\":[\"Four data streams contribute. ARIAscout ran a fresh Shodan sweep on May 12, 2026 to anchor the exposure picture as of publication, not a stale prior-month baseline.\",\" \",[\"$\",\"a\",null,{\"href\":\"https://agentpwn.com\",\"target\":\"_blank\",\"rel\":\"noopener noreferrer\",\"className\":\"text-teal-300 hover:underline\",\"children\":\"AgentPwn\"}],\" \",\"instruments honeypot pages with injection payloads across sector verticals. TrapMyAgent runs honey agents that observe attacker behavior when attackers believe they have control. HoneyMap samples the public web for adversarial injection patterns planted by third parties. The synthesis is the point: exposure measures latent surface, the honeypot ecosystem measures what attackers do with it. Every classification in this report resolves to an\",\" \",[\"$\",\"a\",null,{\"href\":\"https://threats.opena2a.org\",\"target\":\"_blank\",\"rel\":\"noopener noreferrer\",\"className\":\"text-teal-300 hover:underline\",\"children\":\"Agent Threat Matrix\"}],\" \",\"technique identifier in T-NNNN format.\"]}]]}]\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"1c:[\"$\",\"section\",null,{\"className\":\"mb-10\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"h2\",null,{\"className\":\"text-xl font-bold mb-3 text-white\",\"children\":\"1. The volume picture\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"text-gray-300 text-sm mb-4\",\"children\":\"Combined activity across the four streams. Behavioral telemetry is the 30-day window ending May 11. ARIAscout's exposure sweep was run May 12 specifically for this report; the May 12 count is the denominator the rest of this report sits on.\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"space-y-2\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",\"ARIAscout exposed AI services (May 12 sweep)-0\",{\"className\":\"g